comments[1]{created_at,author,text,edited_at}:
  "2026-11-16T23:28:58.941Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation (branch fix/secret-guard-grammar-and-payload-keys): the user_at_private_host local part now starts with a negative lookbehind for [A-Za-z0-9._-] instead of a word boundary, so each run is tried from its first character only and the greedy run backtracks once per run. Measured with findSecretRuleMatches before and after on credential-free input: five pathological inputs of 32 to 48 KB (a- x16000, token- x8000, a. x16000, x_ x16000, a-b@ x8000) took 3,128 ms in total before and stay under the 20 ms per-rule report threshold after; every other rule was already under 20 ms. A run that starts with a dot or hyphen is matched from that character (the new pattern detects a superset of the old one). The spec proves this by comparing against the word-boundary pattern over 1,080 generated spellings (prefix x local part x suffix x three private hosts) and pins linear bounds for 32 KB (under 250 ms in total) and a 512 KB run (under 1 s; quadratic would take minutes). node scripts/check-secrets.mjs stays clean over every tracked file.","2026-11-16T23:29:17.517Z"
